== 6b. DOES '0.020 ruled out in receptions line_pos' SURVIVE A 0.020 EFFECT ON REAL ROWS? (100 game-resampled worlds an arm)
   each world: the 813 real games drawn with replacement (a copy is its own game), real outcomes and the REAL line_pos
   column; then outcomes are moved by d per sd of line_pos (one uniform per player-game: an under flips to over with
   probability d z / (1 - p), an over to under with -d z / p), M.prepare + set_y + analyse_market(line_pos) + holm + verdict.
   The real rows already carry -0.0042, so the world's truth is taken as -0.0042 + the shift the plant achieved (measured
   in the same world, planted minus unplanted). Arm 'to 0.020' sets d = 0.020 - (-0.0042).
   arm              d |  est mean     shift    truth |    Bonf misses   hi < 0.020 EXCLUDED@0.020   sd(est)/SE
   null        0.0000 |   -0.0041   +0.0000  -0.0042 |        0 of 100    100 of 100       71 of 100       1.09
   plus 0.020  0.0200 |   +0.0158   +0.0197  +0.0155 |        0 of 100      3 of 100        3 of 100       1.01
   to 0.020    0.0242 |   +0.0200   +0.0245  +0.0203 |        0 of 100      0 of 100        0 of 100       0.92
   A game-resampled world inherits whatever dependence a game block carries and none that crosses games; it cannot
   show an interval too narrow for a reason the game bootstrap itself ignores (see the season-week blocks in step 2).

